rtion / truncation error:* Increases monotonically as $\\\\alpha \\\\to 0$ (more outlier mass truncated to boundary values).\\n- **Global vs. Layer-wise Stability:** Verify whether a single global fixed $\\\\alpha^*$ maintains stability across all transformer layers or if sensitivity diverges across early vs. late attention layers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### 6. Inquiries on Source Setup Details\\nTo align this experimental design with the exact source methodology (NeurIPS 2024 paper 94328), could you clarify the source-supported specifications for:\\n- **`neurips2024/94328/2:setup_1`**: Exact bit-width configuration (e.g., W4A4KV4, W8A8KV8, or INT4 KV cache with INT8 inputs) and granularity (per-tensor, per-token, or per-channel/head)?\\n- **`neurips2024/94328/2:setup_10`**: The precise clipping formulation (e.g., whether the fixed clipping ratio is shared across inputs and KV cache, or applied per-tensor / per-token) and the tested candidate range?\\n- **`neurips2024/94328/2:setup_17`**: Evaluation benchmarks, token sequence lengths, and baseline reference values reported in the study?\", \"uncertainties\": [\"Precise bit-width assignment across weights, inputs, and KV cache (e.g. 4-bit vs 8-bit) as defined in setup_1.\", \"Exact mathematical parameterization and search grid for the fixed clipping ratio as defined in setup_10.\", \"Specific evaluation corpus splits and context lengths designated as standard benchmarks in setup_17.\"], \"assumptions\": [\"Model architecture under investigation is fixed to LLAMA2-7B (meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-hf).\", \"Quantization is applied dynamically at runtime during inference without re-training or weight parameter updates (post-training quantization setting).\", \"Input activations use symmetric quantization, while KV cache representations use asymmetric quantization with scale and zero-point.\", \"The clipping ratio alpha scales the dynamic activation/KV cache range before computing scale and zero-point factors.\"], \"stage\": \"plan\", 